  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 1234 AM CDT Mon Sep 7 2026\n\nThe long term doesn't look much different than the short term as \nhot, mostly dry, and humid conditions continue through the second \nweek of September. Medium range guidance is starting to hint at a \nfrontal boundary making its way south into north Texas by late this \nweekend and into early next week. For now, this doesn't look like it \nwill cool things off much, however, for what it's worth, but the GFS \nand ECMWF and their ensembles agree that some sort of more effective \npattern change may be in order towards the 3rd weekend of the \nmonth. We will hold out hope for this change as the heat hasn't \nlet up since early August.",
